# A ramp makes the promise of an async function and enters its body. Where the body of an async function awaits the call at once, ResolveAwaitedCalls enters the callee without a promise, so the ramp is not taken into the caller in front of that pass: also where the tests at the head of the callee have just been taken in, and a ramp stands in each of their arms. A promise with another use is made in the caller.
